.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NQHASH 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqhash ,
.Nm nqhini ,
.Nm nqhupd ,
.Nm nqhfin ,
.Nm nqhlen ,
.Nm nqhmac
.Nd SHA-2, SHA-3, SHAKE and HMAC
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft size_t
.Fn nqhlen "nqhalg alg"
.Ft int
.Fo nqhash
.Fa "nqhalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *in" "size_t inlen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn nqhini "nqhctx *ctx" "nqhalg alg"
.Ft int
.Fn nqhupd "nqhctx *ctx" "const uint8_t *in" "size_t inlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqhfin "nqhctx *ctx" "uint8_t *out" "size_t outlen"
.Ft int
.Fo nqhmac
.Fa "nqhalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *key" "size_t keylen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *in" "size_t inlen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Vt nqhalg
names a hash of FIPS 180-4 or FIPS 202:
.Bl -column "NQS512T224" "SHA-512/224" "bytes" -offset indent
.It Sy constant Ta Sy hash Ta Sy bytes
.It Dv NQS224 Ta SHA-224 Ta 28
.It Dv NQS256 Ta SHA-256 Ta 32
.It Dv NQS384 Ta SHA-384 Ta 48
.It Dv NQS512 Ta SHA-512 Ta 64
.It Dv NQS512T224 Ta SHA-512/224 Ta 28
.It Dv NQS512T256 Ta SHA-512/256 Ta 32
.It Dv NQS3224 Ta SHA3-224 Ta 28
.It Dv NQS3256 Ta SHA3-256 Ta 32
.It Dv NQS3384 Ta SHA3-384 Ta 48
.It Dv NQS3512 Ta SHA3-512 Ta 64
.It Dv NQSHK128 Ta SHAKE128 Ta any (32)
.It Dv NQSHK256 Ta SHAKE256 Ta any (64)
.El
.Pp
.Fn nqhlen
returns the digest size in bytes; for SHAKE, the output length the
pre-hash signatures use (32 for SHAKE128, 64 for SHAKE256).
It returns 0 for a value that is not an
.Vt nqhalg .
.Pp
.Fn nqhash
hashes the
.Fa inlen
bytes at
.Fa in
into
.Fa out .
For the fixed-length hashes
.Fa outlen
must be exactly
.Fn nqhlen alg ;
for SHAKE it may be any length, including 0.
.Pp
.Fn nqhini ,
.Fn nqhupd
and
.Fn nqhfin
hash a message given in pieces.
.Vt nqhctx
is opaque but sized in the header, so it can live on the stack; it needs
no cleanup function.
.Fn nqhini
starts
.Fa ctx
for
.Fa alg ;
.Fn nqhupd
absorbs more input and may be called any number of times;
.Fn nqhfin
writes the digest (the same length rule as
.Fn nqhash ) .
For a fixed-length hash,
.Fn nqhfin
ends the context, which must be started again with
.Fn nqhini
before reuse.
For SHAKE,
.Fn nqhfin
may be called again to squeeze more output; after the first
.Fn nqhfin ,
.Fn nqhupd
fails.
.Pp
.Fn nqhmac
computes HMAC (FIPS 198-1, RFC 2104) with any of the ten fixed-length
hashes, writing the first
.Fa outlen
bytes of the tag (1 to
.Fn nqhlen alg )
to
.Fa out .
Compare tags with
.Xr nqcteq 3 ,
never
.Xr memcmp 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn nqhlen
returns a size.
The other functions return
.Dv NQOK
(0) or a negative error code:
.Bl -tag -width NQESTATE
.It Bq Er NQEARG
.Fa alg
is not an
.Vt nqhalg ;
.Fa ctx
is
.Dv NULL ;
a pointer is
.Dv NULL
with a nonzero length;
.Fa outlen
is larger than a fixed-length digest; or, for
.Fn nqhmac ,
.Fa out
is
.Dv NULL
or
.Fa outlen
is 0 or over the digest size.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa outlen
is smaller than a fixed-length digest.
.It Bq Er NQESTATE
.Fn nqhupd
or
.Fn nqhfin
on a context that was not started, or was finished.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fn nqhmac
with SHAKE128 or SHAKE256.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Adapted from
.Pa docs/examples/hash.c
of the source tree:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
const uint8_t abc[] = "abc";
uint8_t d[32], x[64];
nqhctx c;
int rc = nqhash(NQS256, abc, 3, d, sizeof d);
/* SHAKE256: 32 bytes, then 32 more from the same context */
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqhini(&c, NQSHK256);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqhupd(&c, abc, 3);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqhfin(&c, x, 32);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqhfin(&c, x + 32, 32);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-hash 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqcteq 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3
.Sh STANDARDS
FIPS 180-4 (SHA-2), FIPS 202 (SHA-3, SHAKE), FIPS 198-1 (HMAC).
